WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 95 for June 19th, 2026.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.400
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:16.760
CryoEM reveals the full structure of Apobac 3B bound to a viral antagonist showing how

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.740
the enzyme is sequestered into inactive aggregates.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:27.320
The CryoEM structure captures wild-type human Apobac 3B in complex with the Epstein-Barr

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.320
virus protein borough 2.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:36.600
The amino terminal and carboxy terminal domains bridge a borough 2-dimer, creating contacts

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:39.880
that differ from the related factor Apobac 3G.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:47.600
Mutational work indicates the NTD-CTD interaction normally regulates deaminase activity.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:55.200
Borough 2 binding locks the enzyme into large aggregates that prevent cytosine deamination.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:01.060
The structure supplies a template for designing molecules that could block either viral

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.060
evasion or A3B-driven mutagenesis in tumors.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.480
From enzyme-level regulation of mutagenesis, we turn to how nutrient sensing itself shapes

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.300
aging outcomes in a simple model organism.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:22.540
Deletion of SNF1 in Saccharomyces CereVCA alters chronological lifespan in a nutrient-dependent

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:22.880
matter.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.520
Under low glucose and amino acids, the mutant shortens lifespan.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:34.720
Under 5% glucose, plus 3 times amino acids lifespan lengthens, and competitive fitness rises

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.520
by roughly two orders of magnitude in co-culture with wild-type cells.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:44.480
The findings parallel metabolic reprogramming seen in cancer cells.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.980
The same genetic change produces opposite aging outcomes depending on nutrient status.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:56.160
While nutrient sensing governs whole cell lifespan decisions, certain compounds can exploit

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:00.440
similar sensing differences to clear damaged cells selectively.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.920
Work published in aging cells demonstrates that certain antioxidants reduce the burden

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.920
of senescent cells in muscle by changing M2 or signaling.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.720
Senescent cells lose normal nutrient sensing.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.740
The altered pathway appears to push them toward clearance while sparing healthy cells.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:24.520
The selectivity offers a root to lower senescent load without broad cytosycticity.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:30.380
This approach differs from many experimental centerlytics that trigger widespread cell death.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:36.480
From targeted cellular clearance inside muscle, we move outward to how neighborhood design

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.080
itself influences daily movement and long-term emissions.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:47.860
Analysis of U.S. suburban development since 1945 shows neighborhood design features explain

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:52.200
more vehicle miles traveled than simple distance from city centers.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.220
Street patterns that force longer local trips and reduce walking account for a substantial share

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.860
of household carbon output.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.980
The study reframes sprawl policy around street networks rather than density metrics alone.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:12.960
Post-war layouts consistently lengthen routine trips even when homes sit relatively close to amenities.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.540
Southwest Research Institute measurements indicate the inner belt asteroid completes one

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:26.080
end-over-end rotation every 10.5 Earth days while it's spin-axis wobbles every 26.5 days.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.040
The dual-axis motion was detected during the Lucy spacecraft flyby.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:37.000
The finding adds to understanding of how small bodies dissipate rotational energy over time.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:41.520
Lucy data captured the rotation details during the recent encounter.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:48.920
The wobble period of 26.5 days occurs alongside the primary 10.5-day tumble.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:56.000
Researchers note that such dual-axis behavior helps explain energy dissipation patterns in small

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.880
solar system objects. The measurements provide new constraints on how asteroids lose rotational

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:07.840
energy through internal friction and external torques. The intersection of the San Andreas and

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.220
Jacinto faults at Cahon Pass now carries the highest stress recorded in the last 1000 years.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.280
Researchers mapped stress accumulation and identified the past as a structural feature that can

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:26.700
either stop or allow rupture to propagate across both faults. Conditions match those preceding

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:32.780
several of the region's largest historical events. The current stress level exceeds values documented

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:39.780
across the preceding millennium of geologic records. Mapping shows the past functions as a gate that

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:46.240
may permit or halt rupture transfer between the two major faults. Historical events in the area

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:51.780
occurred under comparable stress states at the same location. The findings come from direct

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:58.080
measurements of accumulated strain in the fault network. Emerging studies link heavy device use to

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:04.280
measurable declines in attention and mood, yet no evidence supports the idea that brains physically

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:11.380
deteriorate from screen time. The phrase brain rot captures real cognitive and emotional costs rather

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:17.320
than structural decay. Researchers emphasized distinguishing correlation from direct causation

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:23.800
in future work. Heavy screen exposure correlates with reduced focus and lowered mood scores across

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:30.820
multiple cohorts. No imaging or histological data indicate actual tissue level brain changes from

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:37.540
device use alone. The term brain rot therefore functions as shorthand for functional impacts rather

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:44.180
than literal damage. Future studies are urged to separate usage patterns from other lifestyle variables

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:51.200
that affect attention and affect. University of Manchester analysis of the EU deforestation-free

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:58.100
products regulation finds mismatches between regulatory requirements and actual beef supply chains

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:04.340
in Brazil. Traceability and enforcement shortfalls could limit the policy's impact on tropical

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:10.740
forest loss. The study highlights challenges the UK would face if adopting similar import rules.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:17.500
Brazilian beef supply chains show incomplete documentation that falls short of EU traceability

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:23.500
standards. Enforcement gaps at multiple points in the chain reduce the regulation's ability to

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:29.940
curb forest conversion. The analysis identifies specific points where data on origin and land use

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:36.260
history remain unavailable. Comparable import policies considered by the UK would encounter the

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:43.280
same traceability obstacles documented in the Brazilian case. A review of device data in patients with

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:49.760
established cardiovascular disease finds inconsistent effects on clinical outcomes. Some studies

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.880
report improved medication adherence while others show no change in hospitalizations or mortality.

00:06:56.780 --> 00:07:00.180
Larger trials are needed to clarify which patient groups benefit.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:05.920
Wearable devices produce variable results across existing cardiovascular cohorts.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:12.420
Medication taking behavior improves in certain monitored groups yet shows no corresponding drop in

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:18.200
hospital admissions. Mortality rates remain unchanged in the majority of reviewed trials.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:24.440
The review concludes that targeted studies must identify subgroups where device feedback translates

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:31.600
into measurable clinical gains. A new survey indicates only about half of US adults had both affordable

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:37.600
and high quality healthcare last year. The share reporting access difficulties has increased compared

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:45.000
with prior years. Cost barriers remain the dominant reason cited. Roughly 50% of respondents obtained care

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:51.900
meeting both affordability and quality criteria. The proportion facing access problems has risen steadily

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:57.900
across successive survey waves. Cost remains the leading factor preventing people from receiving

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:03.760
needed services. The findings reflect responses collected from a nationally representative sample of

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:10.600
the alliance for longevity initiatives white paper outlines a multi-disease therapeutic designation

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:15.900
that would allow sponsors to pursue one approval covering multiple age-related conditions

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:23.260
sharing a mechanism. Section 6 addresses potential regulatory objections. The approach aims to reduce

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:29.780
the need for sequential indication expansions. Sponsors could seek a single designation for therapies

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:37.120
acting on shared aging pathways. The white paper section 6 responds directly to anticipated FDA

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:43.220
concerns about the multi-disease framework. Sequential approvals for each indication would no

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:49.740
longer be required under the proposed pathway. The designation is intended to streamline development

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:56.740
for interventions targeting common biological drivers of age-related disease. University of Auckland

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:03.080
researchers who developed the R language have been honored with an award described as the Nobel Prize

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:09.980
for statisticians. The recognition highlights R's role in enabling reproducible analysis across

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:16.680
biomedical and environmental research. The award acknowledges contributions that underpins statistical

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:23.580
workflows in multiple scientific domains. R has become a standard platform for reproducible data

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:30.200
analysis in laboratories worldwide. Biomedical and environmental studies frequently rely on

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:36.800
R packages for statistical validation and visualization. The honor underscores the language's

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:41.780
influence on research practices that require transparent code and data handling.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:47.980
University of Auckland team members received the award for sustained development of the open source

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:54.680
tool. From built environment influences on daily behavior, we close with a methodological tool that

00:09:54.680 --> 00:10:01.140
quietly enables much of today's reproducible biology. Now, here's something most people get wrong

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:07.980
about antioxidants. Most people assume antioxidants simply shield every cell from oxidative damage

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:14.920
in the same way. In reality, they can selectively push certain damage cells toward removal while

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:21.300
leaving healthy ones untouched. Right now, as you move, your muscle fibers contain a small population

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:28.640
of senescent cells that have lost normal nutrient sensing. Antioxidants appear to exploit that difference

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:35.280
by shifting m-tore signaling and tipping those cells into clearance. One memorable detail is that

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:40.660
this selectivity occurs without the broad cell death seen with many experimental senolytics.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:47.620
A practical takeaway is to watch for trials that test whether particular antioxidant doses or timing

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:53.320
produce measurable drops in senescent markers, rather than general antioxidant claims.

